Read every boolean in the config with one token set

readBoolEntry accepts the exact token true and reads every other value
as false. toLvLines reads every value except the literal false as true.
The one file therefore holds two boolean grammars, and both disagree
with KConfig, the writer of the file.

A hand edited value such as 1, on or TRUE switches an option off, and
any hostile token switches the list view lines on.

Add toBool with the token set of KConfig, and route both readers through
it. The parser reads true, yes, on and 1 as true, and false, no, off and
0 as false, in any letter case. An unknown token now gives the default
of the key, which no reader gave before. The writer emits only true and
false, so no written file changes its meaning.

A reader oracle reads 1, yes, on and TRUE as true on two boolean keys.
It reads 0, no, off and zzqq on lvLines as false, where the old reader
read all four as true.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 4 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 1073777e..0f18e278 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -392,6 +392,20 @@ static EGradType toGradType(const char *str, EGradType def)
     return def;
 }
 
+// Read one boolean value with the token set of KConfig, the writer of the
+// file. An empty value and an unknown token give def.
+static bool toBool(const char *str, bool def)
+{
+    if(str && 0!=str[0])
+    {
+        if(QtCurve::oneOf<QtCurve::CaseCmp>(str, "true", "yes", "on", "1"))
+            return true;
+        if(QtCurve::oneOf<QtCurve::CaseCmp>(str, "false", "no", "off", "0"))
+            return false;
+    }
+    return def;
+}
+
 static bool toLvLines(const char *str, bool def)
 {
     if(str && 0!=str[0])
@@ -404,7 +418,7 @@ static bool toLvLines(const char *str, bool def)
         if(0==strncmp(str, "false", 5) || 0==strncmp(str, "none", 4))
             return LV_NONE;
 #else
-        return 0!=strncmp(str, "false", 5);
+        return toBool(str, def);
 #endif
     }
     return def;
@@ -718,7 +732,7 @@ static bool readBoolEntry(QtCConfig &cfg, const QString &key, bool def)
 {
     const QString &val(readStringEntry(cfg, key));
 
-    return val.isEmpty() ? def : (val==QLatin1String("true") ? true : false);
+    return toBool(TO_LATIN1(val), def);
 }
 
